story:AtlasStaple
  Styles
  Plan
  Opt
    For
  EntropyArrest
    Entcase:Self_round
      lematch,self,round
        means,spayer,re:self.round={INT},tol:any
  step,dige:c395d6a2c0dd07c7
  step=2,desc:load Ghost/L/Atlas.g on demand — mint A:Atlas beside the run — aim it at the frozen fixture,dige:0c14a558d5c4c94a
    Assertion:the-atlas-ghost-loads,sentence:the Atlas ghost loads on demand — no CREDULER_GHOSTS manifest edit needed
    Assertion:atlas-maps-a-real,sentence:Atlas maps a real doc in its fixture corpus
    Assertion:the-map-lists-every,sentence:the Map lists every def the fixture actually declares
    Assertion:every-call-in-the,sentence:every call in the fixture carries its enclosing def as via
  step=3,desc:inject an unreadable Doc row — the error path must mark it and never spin forever,dige:ee4924448d615915
    Assertion:an-unreadable-path-records,sentence:an unreadable path records an error and does not spin forever
  step=4,desc:stamp a stale mapper on the real doc — a re-map must replace its Map and never pile a second,dige:bd06b494d3971362
    Assertion:a-re-map-under-a,sentence:a re-map under a fresh mapper version replaces the Map — never piles a second one
  step=5,desc:write a file into the corpus — change it — delete it: each refresh must find and re-map and drop,dige:a1796afec39cdf40
    Assertion:a-file-written-after,sentence:a file written after the roster is found and mapped by the next refresh
    Assertion:a-file-that-changed,sentence:a file that changed under a settled Doc is re-mapped by the next refresh
    Assertion:a-file-deleted-from,sentence:a file deleted from the corpus drops out of the census on the next refresh
  step=6,desc:drop A:Atlas and stand it again — the fixture doc must come back warm from the cache with its Map intact,dige:9b6897b657b1f7fd
    Assertion:a-re-stood-atlas-warms,sentence:a re-stood Atlas warms its Map from the cache — no read and no parse
